Mental Note:
Currently we have 4 components(Races, Race, Pony, and Menue) beside the default app component.

Let's create a mental map for our compenents or how the data flows between our components:

                        App Component/ App template 
                        (parent to Races and Menu)
                        |                       |
                        |                       |
                        |                       |
                        |                       v
                        |                   Menu component
                        |
                        v
                Races component ---------> RaceModel
                (parent to Race)
                        |
                        |
                        |
                        v
                Race component ----------> RaceModel
                (parent to Pony)
                        |
                        |
                        |
                        v
                Pony component ----------> PonyModel


In the above map, We should remember that:
    1️⃣The term "A is parent to B" means that the selector of B is used inside the template of A
        eg: Races component is the parent component of Race component means
            selector of Race component(pr-race) is used inside the template of component Races(races.html)

            Inside races.html:

                @for (race of races(); track race.id) {
                    <div>
                        <!-- <h2>{{ race.name }}</h2> -->
                        <pr-race [raceModel]="race" /> 👈
                    </div>
                }


Also let's quickly look back to our interfaces: RaceModel implements PonyModel.

    RaceModel:
        export interface RaceModel {
            id: number;
            name: string;
            ponies: Array<PonyModel>;
            startInstant: string;
        }


    PonyModel:
        export interface PonyModel {
            id: number;
            name: string;
            color: string;
        }


Also let's see the snippent of our components templates just to get the idea behind displaying the
races and ponies:

    app.html:
        <pr-menu /> 👈
        <main class="container" style="margin-top: 70px">
            <h1>Ponyracer</h1>
            <pr-races /> 👈
        </main>


    races.html:
        @for (race of races(); track race.id) {
            <div>
                <pr-race [raceModel]="race" /> 👈
            </div>
        }
    

    race.html:
        <div>
            <h2>{{ raceModel().name }}</h2>
            <div class="row">
                @for (pony of raceModel().ponies; track pony.id) {
                    <div class="col-sm-2">
                        <pr-pony [ponyModel]="pony" /> 👈
                    </div>
                }
        </div>


    pony.html:
        <figure (click)="selectPony()">
            <img [src]="ponyImageUrl()" [alt]="ponyModel().name" />
            <figcaption>{{ ponyModel().name }}</figcaption>
        </figure>


From the templates above, we should know that:
    🔥 Pony component is responsible for displaying singly pony hence name Pony and not Ponies.
    🔥 Race component is responsible for displaying a series/list of pony hence ponies under the race
        name. Note that we used pony selector inside the for loop in race template.
    🔥 Races component is responsible for displaying a series/list of race hence races. Note that we
        used race selector containing a race name and a series/list of pony inside the for loop in
        races component.


Now, per instruction, we should display the startInstant using date pipe. But where do we code for
doing so? At this point, it's obvious that it should be inside race component because that's where the
race with name and ponies is. Also Race component uses RaceModel which has a property startInstant
mentioned in he instruction. plus the instruction itself says so.


Now the only thing left to do import the DatePipe in Race component in order to use the date pipe inside
the Race template(race.html). Next we will use the date pipe to display the start instant in a short
format in a p tag below the title(race name):

    <h2>{{ raceModel().name }}</h2>
    <p>{{ raceModel().startInstant | date: 'short' }}</p>